+### 2132 — Common SSH conformance remains fixture-level for the deferred candidate (TASK-260715-2d3g5e)
+- TESTS: One Swift Testing suite now selects libssh2 and ReluxNIOSSH registrations as data and runs the same M0 assertions for host-before-auth ordering, approved algorithms/authentication, direct/exec/upload bounds, partial writes and half-close/reset/cancel behavior, byte/time/test/manual/server rekey, keepalive, all reviewed cancellation sites, lifecycle baselines, metrics, privacy sentinels, and explicit M3 states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
+- SCOPE: Both registrations are deterministic candidate fixtures. They prove the common harness and contract without candidate-specific exceptions; they are not production adapter or real-server matrix evidence. The production libssh2 loopback suite remains green, while the ReluxNIOSSH production adapter remains intentionally deferred by ADR-014 and `TASK-260715-1af33i`.
+- VERIFICATION: 429 Swift tests in 36 suites pass; affected-file coverage is 89.27% regions, 87.07% functions, and 96.88% lines. Recursive Swift format lint, core-boundary validation, and `swift build` exit 0.
